@startuml
title TMFC027 : Product Configurator -- eTOM/SID ABE Links

package "TMFC027 - Product Configurator" {
  class "L2 - Product Configuration Management" as L2ProductConfigurationManagement <<eTOM Business Activity>>
  class "Product Configuration*" as ProductConfiguration_TMFC027 <<SID Data Entity>>
}

package "TMFC001 - Product Catalog" {
  class "Product Offering" as ProductOffering_TMFC001 <<SID Data Entity>>
  class "Party Product Spec. & Offering" as PartyProductSpecOffering_TMFC001 <<SID Data Entity>>
  class "Product Specification" as ProductSpecification_TMFC001 <<SID Data Entity>>
  class "Product Configuration**" as ProductConfiguration_TMFC001 <<SID Data Entity>>
}

package "TMFC005 - Product Inventory" {
  class "Product" as Product_TMFC005 <<SID Data Entity>>
}

note bottom
  *only Product Configuration BEs
  **only Product Configuration Spec
end note

' Per the image's own legend: an arrow from the eTOM activity towards a SID ABE
' means the information is produced by the activity; the arrow in the other
' direction means the information is consumed by the activity. Only the three
' arrows the source image actually draws are reproduced here -- "Product
' Offering" and "Party Product Spec. & Offering" (both in the TMFC001 box) and
' "Product Configuration**" are shown in the image but are NOT connected by any
' arrow; only "Product Specification" (TMFC001) and "Product" (TMFC005) link to
' the activity.
L2ProductConfigurationManagement --> ProductConfiguration_TMFC027 : produces
ProductSpecification_TMFC001 --> L2ProductConfigurationManagement : is consumed by
Product_TMFC005 --> L2ProductConfigurationManagement : is consumed by

@enduml
